{"full":"hf:latentexplorers/latent-collider","spaceId":"latentexplorers/latent-collider","name":"Latent Collider","source":"huggingface","description":"Drag concept nodes to morph a FLUX image in real time","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":3,"created":"2026-06-08T16:20:42.000Z","updated":"2026-06-08T16:24:01.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://latentexplorers-latent-collider.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/latentexplorers/latent-collider","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:31.472Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:31.472Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:31.472Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🪐","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A magenta-collider-style node field for navigating FLUX latent space.","Drag concept nodes around the central output image. Each node's pull on the image is its inverse-square distance to the center, normalized across all nodes. Those weights blend the concepts' text embeddings (pooled CLIP + T5 sequence), and FLUX.1-schnell renders the blend — so the image morphs in near-real-time as you move nodes.","Built on the embedding-steering idea from latentexplorers/latentnavigation-flux, re-skinned with the interactive node UI from the Magenta RT Image Collider."],"features":["Real-time: a long-lived ZeroGPU grant runs a generation loop that re-renders whenever the blend","Fast: FLUX.1-schnell (4 steps) + the TAEF1 tiny autoencoder, 512×512 by default."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/latentexplorers/latent-collider/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1ca44d40e3ed99f3feda919d0bd2045b37c315facd8eb9b8f16904edd321ba51","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:31.527Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:31.527Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A magenta-collider-style node field for navigating FLUX latent space.","sourceUrl":"https: